1
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:04,600
I'm Peppa Pig.

2
00:00:04,666 --> 00:00:05,533
[oinks]

3
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:07,266
This is my little brother, George.

4
00:00:07,333 --> 00:00:08,200
[oinks]

5
00:00:08,266 --> 00:00:09,433
This is Mommy Pig.

6
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:10,366
[oinks]

7
00:00:10,433 --> 00:00:11,733
And this is Daddy Pig.

8
00:00:11,799 --> 00:00:12,666
[oinks loudly]

9
00:00:12,733 --> 00:00:14,200
[all laugh]

10
00:00:14,266 --> 00:00:15,166
Peppa Pig.

11
00:00:16,433 --> 00:00:18,300
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

12
00:00:18,366 --> 00:00:20,466
[narrator] It is a lovely sunny morning.

13
00:00:20,533 --> 00:00:23,066
Daddy Pig is driving to work in his car.

14
00:00:24,366 --> 00:00:26,066
Breakfast time, Goldie.

15
00:00:26,133 --> 00:00:28,533
[narrator]
Mommy Pig is feeding Goldie the Fish.

16
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:32,333
Mommy, Goldie isn't eating.

17
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:34,666
Oh, maybe she's not feeling very well.

18
00:00:34,733 --> 00:00:36,699
Let's phone Dr. Hamster the Vet.

19
00:00:38,233 --> 00:00:39,800
[phone ringing]

20
00:00:42,233 --> 00:00:44,600
Dr. Hamster the Vet speaking.

21
00:00:44,666 --> 00:00:46,199
[Mommy Pig] Hello, Dr. Hamster.

22
00:00:46,266 --> 00:00:48,466
Goldie the Fish is not eating.

23
00:00:48,533 --> 00:00:50,633
And she looks sad.

24
00:00:50,699 --> 00:00:54,266
Oh, you'd better bring Goldie
to see me right away.

25
00:00:55,699 --> 00:00:59,000
Oh. Daddy took the car.

26
00:00:59,066 --> 00:01:01,199
How do we get to the vet?

27
00:01:01,266 --> 00:01:02,766
We can take the bus.

28
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:04,633
Oh, goody.

29
00:01:06,300 --> 00:01:07,733
[narrator] This is the bus stop.

30
00:01:07,800 --> 00:01:11,800
The timetable says the next bus
will be here at 10:00.

31
00:01:12,033 --> 00:01:13,800
What time is it now?

32
00:01:14,033 --> 00:01:15,233
Ten o'clock.

33
00:01:15,800 --> 00:01:17,233
-Hooray!
-Hooray!

34
00:01:17,300 --> 00:01:18,433
[laughing]

35
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:20,133
How many tickets?

36
00:01:20,333 --> 00:01:25,100
-One mommy ticket and two little piggies.
-And one fish, please.

37
00:01:25,166 --> 00:01:26,600
The fish goes free.

38
00:01:28,133 --> 00:01:29,433
[laughing]

39
00:01:30,633 --> 00:01:32,000
Hold tight.

40
00:01:33,366 --> 00:01:35,366
[narrator]
Mr. Bull is waiting for the bus.

41
00:01:38,199 --> 00:01:39,433
Moo!

42
00:01:39,500 --> 00:01:42,666
One ticket to the music shop, please.

43
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:47,199
Hello, Mr. Bull.

44
00:01:47,500 --> 00:01:50,333
We're taking Goldie to the vet.

45
00:01:50,399 --> 00:01:51,666
Oh, dear.

46
00:01:51,733 --> 00:01:54,100
Feeling poorly, are we, Goldie?

47
00:01:54,166 --> 00:01:56,699
She can't talk. She's a fish.

48
00:01:56,766 --> 00:01:58,000
Of course.

49
00:01:58,066 --> 00:02:02,566
Uh, maybe she'd like to hear a tune
on my tuba?

50
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:04,666
[honking]

51
00:02:06,500 --> 00:02:08,133
It sounds funny.

52
00:02:08,199 --> 00:02:12,400
That's why I'm going to the music shop
to get it mended.

53
00:02:12,466 --> 00:02:13,799
Ooh!

54
00:02:15,266 --> 00:02:20,233
[narrator] Mrs. Sheep, Mrs. Cat, Mr. Zebra
and Madame Gazelle have got on the bus.

55
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:23,533
Four tickets to the supermarket, please.

56
00:02:26,233 --> 00:02:28,100
Hello, Madame Gazelle.

57
00:02:28,166 --> 00:02:31,000
We're taking Goldie to the vet.

58
00:02:31,066 --> 00:02:33,633
Oh, is Goldie not well?

59
00:02:35,166 --> 00:02:37,000
She likes you.

60
00:02:37,799 --> 00:02:40,766
The wheels on the bus
Go round and round

61
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:43,400
Round and round, round and round

62
00:02:43,466 --> 00:02:46,066
The wheels on the bus
Go round and round

63
00:02:46,133 --> 00:02:49,000
All day long

64
00:02:49,066 --> 00:02:50,500
[laughing]

65
00:02:50,600 --> 00:02:52,166
Supermarket.

66
00:02:52,799 --> 00:02:53,766
Bye.

67
00:02:54,766 --> 00:02:56,266
Music shop.

68
00:02:57,366 --> 00:02:58,500
Bye.

69
00:02:59,166 --> 00:03:01,266
Last stop, the vet.

70
00:03:03,033 --> 00:03:05,166
[narrator]
The vet helps sick pets get better.

71
00:03:05,533 --> 00:03:07,799
[squawking and croaking]

72
00:03:08,066 --> 00:03:11,166
Aw. Is this the sad little fish
that won't eat?

73
00:03:11,233 --> 00:03:12,633
Yes. Watch this.

74
00:03:15,466 --> 00:03:19,533
-[narrator] Goldie has eaten the food.
-Oh, she didn't eat at home.

75
00:03:19,600 --> 00:03:22,600
Maybe Goldie was bored at home.

76
00:03:22,666 --> 00:03:25,600
The interesting journey
has cheered her up.

77
00:03:25,666 --> 00:03:26,600
Oh!

78
00:03:26,666 --> 00:03:30,233
You have a very healthy, happy fish.

79
00:03:30,299 --> 00:03:31,533
She's lovely.

80
00:03:31,600 --> 00:03:34,299
Thank you, Dr. Hamster.

81
00:03:35,033 --> 00:03:38,600
[narrator] Mommy Pig, Peppa and George
are going home on the bus.

82
00:03:40,100 --> 00:03:43,200
Mr. Bull is going home
with his mended tuba.

83
00:03:43,733 --> 00:03:45,766
It's as good as new.

84
00:03:46,100 --> 00:03:48,166
[playing notes]

85
00:03:48,700 --> 00:03:49,700
[laughing]

86
00:03:50,700 --> 00:03:54,700
[narrator] Madame Gazelle and her friends
are going home with their shopping.

87
00:03:56,399 --> 00:03:59,000
I see Goldie the Fish is happy again.

88
00:03:59,066 --> 00:04:03,066
Yes. It was the bus ride
that made her better.

89
00:04:03,333 --> 00:04:06,200
The fish in the bowl swims round and round

90
00:04:06,366 --> 00:04:08,633
Round and round, round and round

91
00:04:08,700 --> 00:04:11,666
The fish in the bowl swims round and round

92
00:04:11,733 --> 00:04:14,233
All day long

93
00:04:14,299 --> 00:04:15,799
[all laughing]

94
00:04:16,466 --> 00:04:18,399
Hello. Where have you been?

95
00:04:18,466 --> 00:04:22,766
We took Goldie to the vet,
and now she's better.

96
00:04:23,200 --> 00:04:24,133
[coughing]

97
00:04:24,200 --> 00:04:26,300
[narrator] Oh, dear, Goldie has a cough.

98
00:04:27,200 --> 00:04:30,099
We should take Goldie
to the vet again tomorrow.

99
00:04:30,166 --> 00:04:32,500
-I can drive you in the car.
-No, Daddy.

100
00:04:32,566 --> 00:04:35,566
We want to go on the bus. It's fun.

101
00:04:35,633 --> 00:04:38,099
Okay. We'll go on the bus.

102
00:04:38,166 --> 00:04:39,333
Hooray!

103
00:04:40,300 --> 00:04:45,266
[narrator] Everyone loves going on
the bus, especially Goldie the Fish.

104
00:04:49,033 --> 00:04:50,400
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

105
00:04:50,466 --> 00:04:53,633
[narrator] Today, Peppa and her family
have come to the Funfair.

106
00:04:54,500 --> 00:04:56,733
I love the Funfair.

107
00:04:57,333 --> 00:04:59,000
Slidey, slidey.

108
00:04:59,066 --> 00:05:01,666
[Daddy Pig]
George wants to go on the helter-skelter.

109
00:05:01,733 --> 00:05:04,800
-Okay, see you later.
-See you later.

110
00:05:05,433 --> 00:05:06,700
Roll up, roll up.

111
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:09,800
Hook a duck and win a giant teddy.

112
00:05:10,033 --> 00:05:13,066
-Mommy, can we have a go?
-Okay.

113
00:05:13,533 --> 00:05:16,266
-One pound, please.
-One pound?

114
00:05:16,333 --> 00:05:18,133
It's all for a good cause.

115
00:05:18,666 --> 00:05:20,700
Win the giant teddy, Mommy.

116
00:05:20,766 --> 00:05:24,266
I'll try, Peppa,
but I don't think it's that easy.

117
00:05:24,333 --> 00:05:26,433
You're right. You've got no chance.

118
00:05:26,500 --> 00:05:28,500
-What?
-It's impossible.

119
00:05:28,566 --> 00:05:30,500
Waste of money, if you ask me.

120
00:05:30,566 --> 00:05:31,800
We'll see about that.

121
00:05:34,466 --> 00:05:35,766
[narrator] Mommy Pig has won.

122
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:36,700
Hooray!

123
00:05:36,766 --> 00:05:38,400
That's amazing.

124
00:05:38,466 --> 00:05:40,000
Here's your giant teddy.

125
00:05:40,066 --> 00:05:42,500
Wouldn't you like a little teddy instead?

126
00:05:42,566 --> 00:05:44,633
No way, Jose.

127
00:05:45,366 --> 00:05:48,666
Look, Mommy, a giant teddy.

128
00:05:48,733 --> 00:05:50,333
It's a bit big.

129
00:05:50,400 --> 00:05:52,266
No, it's not.

130
00:05:53,533 --> 00:05:57,300
[narrator] George and Daddy Pig
are queuing for the helter-skelter.

131
00:05:57,633 --> 00:06:02,466
Mm. It's a bit high, George.
Are you sure you want to have a go?

132
00:06:02,533 --> 00:06:03,599
[oinks]

133
00:06:03,666 --> 00:06:05,599
One pound, please.

134
00:06:05,666 --> 00:06:07,066
One pound?

135
00:06:07,133 --> 00:06:09,433
It's all for a good cause.

136
00:06:10,599 --> 00:06:12,099
[laughing]

137
00:06:16,800 --> 00:06:18,000
[crying]

138
00:06:18,066 --> 00:06:21,166
[narrator]
Oh, dear. It is a bit too high for George.

139
00:06:21,233 --> 00:06:24,433
Don't worry, George,
I'll come up with you.

140
00:06:24,500 --> 00:06:27,633
-That's 1 pound, please.
-Oh.

141
00:06:32,700 --> 00:06:35,366
[narrator]
George isn't afraid of heights anymore.

142
00:06:35,433 --> 00:06:36,299
Oh.

143
00:06:36,766 --> 00:06:38,633
It is a bit high, isn't it?

144
00:06:39,099 --> 00:06:40,766
I'll just go down the stairs.

145
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:43,133
[narrator]
The stairs are full of children.

146
00:06:44,033 --> 00:06:46,466
That's the way down, Daddy Pig.

147
00:06:47,099 --> 00:06:48,700
Oh. Okay.

148
00:06:49,066 --> 00:06:50,733
Whoa!

149
00:06:52,433 --> 00:06:54,099
[all laughing]

150
00:06:54,599 --> 00:06:56,099
Roll up, roll up.

151
00:06:56,166 --> 00:07:00,033
Hit the target and win a giant teddy.

152
00:07:01,566 --> 00:07:03,666
You can do that easy, Mommy.

153
00:07:03,733 --> 00:07:06,500
We don't want to win
another giant teddy.

154
00:07:06,566 --> 00:07:09,166
Don't worry, you won't win.

155
00:07:09,233 --> 00:07:11,133
Women are useless at this.

156
00:07:11,200 --> 00:07:12,799
I'm sorry, what did you say?

157
00:07:13,033 --> 00:07:14,733
It's a game of skill.

158
00:07:15,133 --> 00:07:16,666
How much for one go?

159
00:07:17,299 --> 00:07:18,166
One pound.

160
00:07:21,566 --> 00:07:23,033
[narrator] Mommy Pig has won.

161
00:07:23,099 --> 00:07:24,500
Unbelievable.

162
00:07:24,566 --> 00:07:26,433
Here's your giant teddy.

163
00:07:26,500 --> 00:07:27,466
Hooray!

164
00:07:27,533 --> 00:07:30,433
I want a teddy like that one, Mommy.

165
00:07:30,500 --> 00:07:32,000
They're too big.

166
00:07:32,066 --> 00:07:33,666
No, they're not.

167
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:38,533
[narrator] Daddy Pig and George
are riding on the Big Wheel.

168
00:07:38,599 --> 00:07:40,200
Hold tight now.

169
00:07:41,233 --> 00:07:43,333
That really is high.

170
00:07:43,799 --> 00:07:45,799
Whoa!

171
00:07:46,599 --> 00:07:49,166
Phew. I'm glad that's over.

172
00:07:49,633 --> 00:07:52,500
Five times round for 1 pound.

173
00:07:52,566 --> 00:07:54,533
Five times round?

174
00:07:54,599 --> 00:07:56,099
Oh, no.

175
00:07:56,266 --> 00:07:58,166
Whoa!

176
00:07:59,400 --> 00:08:01,066
Roll up, roll up.

177
00:08:01,266 --> 00:08:05,666
Test your strength
on the old Hammer and Bell.

178
00:08:05,733 --> 00:08:07,166
What do we have to do?

179
00:08:07,233 --> 00:08:10,533
You hit this button with this hammer.

180
00:08:10,599 --> 00:08:13,733
If the bell rings, you win a prize.

181
00:08:14,500 --> 00:08:15,533
[dings]

182
00:08:15,599 --> 00:08:19,366
No skill involved,
but you need to be strong.

183
00:08:19,566 --> 00:08:21,000
I'll have a go.

184
00:08:21,066 --> 00:08:22,166
One pound.

185
00:08:26,666 --> 00:08:28,000
Bad luck.

186
00:08:28,066 --> 00:08:29,133
Oh, ho.

187
00:08:29,200 --> 00:08:30,466
I'm strong.

188
00:08:30,533 --> 00:08:32,166
I'll have a go.

189
00:08:33,133 --> 00:08:35,199
Stand back, everyone.

190
00:08:35,266 --> 00:08:37,100
Do be careful, Daddy Pig.

191
00:08:37,333 --> 00:08:38,566
You're not that fit.

192
00:08:39,366 --> 00:08:43,199
-Yes, Daddy Pig is looking a bit tubby.
-What?

193
00:08:43,266 --> 00:08:47,000
I'm just saying Daddy Pig
is a bit round in the tummy.

194
00:08:47,433 --> 00:08:49,466
Give me that hammer.

195
00:08:55,433 --> 00:08:56,633
Goodness me.

196
00:08:57,000 --> 00:08:59,166
I've never seen anything like it.

197
00:08:59,233 --> 00:09:02,133
That wins all the giant teddies we have.

198
00:09:02,199 --> 00:09:03,166
Hooray!

199
00:09:03,366 --> 00:09:06,533
Mommy, can we give these teddies
to my friends?

200
00:09:06,600 --> 00:09:08,300
What a good idea.

201
00:09:08,766 --> 00:09:10,300
Thank you, Peppa.

202
00:09:10,366 --> 00:09:11,666
Most kind.

203
00:09:11,733 --> 00:09:13,500
Thank you very much.

204
00:09:13,566 --> 00:09:15,300
[all laughing]

205
00:09:20,500 --> 00:09:22,233
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

206
00:09:22,300 --> 00:09:25,066
[narrator] It is a school day for Peppa
and her friends.

207
00:09:25,566 --> 00:09:30,633
Children, today,
we will be learning all about numbers.

208
00:09:31,199 --> 00:09:34,466
Does anybody know what numbers are for?

209
00:09:35,100 --> 00:09:37,266
Are numbers for counting?

210
00:09:37,333 --> 00:09:40,633
Yes, Peppa.
Who would like to do some counting now?

211
00:09:40,699 --> 00:09:43,333
[all] Me. Me. Me.

212
00:09:43,400 --> 00:09:44,733
Okay, Pedro.

213
00:09:44,800 --> 00:09:50,066
Uh. One, two, three, four.

214
00:09:50,333 --> 00:09:52,366
[narrator] Pedro has counted to four.

215
00:09:52,433 --> 00:09:53,766
Well done, Pedro.

216
00:09:55,466 --> 00:09:58,133
Can anyone count higher than four?

217
00:09:58,199 --> 00:09:59,733
Me, me, me.

218
00:09:59,800 --> 00:10:00,699
Rebecca.

219
00:10:01,333 --> 00:10:06,100
One, two, three, four, five, six, seven.

220
00:10:06,166 --> 00:10:09,633
-[narrator] Rebecca has counted to seven.
-Excellent, Rebecca.

221
00:10:11,233 --> 00:10:12,533
Madame Gazelle.

222
00:10:12,600 --> 00:10:14,066
Yes, Candy?

223
00:10:14,133 --> 00:10:16,233
My mom can count to 10.

224
00:10:16,300 --> 00:10:18,000
[all] Wow. 

225
00:10:18,066 --> 00:10:22,766
Yes, after seven,
there is eight, nine, ten.

226
00:10:23,400 --> 00:10:25,800
[all] Eight, nine, ten.

227
00:10:26,033 --> 00:10:27,333
Very good.

228
00:10:29,266 --> 00:10:30,500
[narrator] It is playtime.

229
00:10:32,699 --> 00:10:37,066
Rebecca Rabbit, Zoë Zebra,
Suzy Sheep and Peppa all like to skip.

230
00:10:37,633 --> 00:10:39,333
I like sand

231
00:10:39,633 --> 00:10:41,233
I like sea

232
00:10:41,633 --> 00:10:45,400
I like Suzy to skip with me

233
00:10:45,466 --> 00:10:46,733
[laughing]

234
00:10:46,800 --> 00:10:48,533
I like ping

235
00:10:48,600 --> 00:10:50,333
I like pong

236
00:10:50,400 --> 00:10:53,300
I like Zoë to skip along

237
00:10:54,800 --> 00:10:55,666
I know.

238
00:10:55,733 --> 00:10:59,166
Let's see who can skip the most
without stopping.

239
00:11:00,100 --> 00:11:01,166
I'll count.

240
00:11:01,666 --> 00:11:06,266
One, two, three, four, five,

241
00:11:06,500 --> 00:11:11,066
six, seven, eight, nine, ten.

242
00:11:11,566 --> 00:11:14,133
Zoë wins. Hooray!

243
00:11:14,600 --> 00:11:16,133
-Hooray.
-Hooray.

244
00:11:18,333 --> 00:11:21,400
Pedro, do you want
to do some skipping?

245
00:11:21,466 --> 00:11:25,100
No thanks, Peppa,
I'm Hula-Hooping.

246
00:11:25,166 --> 00:11:28,600
Wibble Wobble, Wibble Wobble
Wiggle Waggle Wee

247
00:11:28,666 --> 00:11:32,466
Hula-Hoop, Hula-Hoop
One, two, three

248
00:11:32,666 --> 00:11:34,266
Ooh.

249
00:11:34,333 --> 00:11:37,133
How many can you do without stopping?

250
00:11:37,199 --> 00:11:39,333
A million and three.

251
00:11:39,400 --> 00:11:41,633
Wow, that's a lot.

252
00:11:41,699 --> 00:11:44,000
Let's count them.

253
00:11:44,466 --> 00:11:50,066
One, two, three, four,
five, six, seven, eight--

254
00:11:50,533 --> 00:11:52,300
That was eight.

255
00:11:52,366 --> 00:11:54,133
I'm a bit tired.

256
00:11:54,199 --> 00:11:56,433
I'll do the rest later.

257
00:11:56,500 --> 00:11:58,166
[trumpets then laughs]

258
00:11:58,566 --> 00:12:01,333
Can you do Hula-Hoops, Emily?

259
00:12:01,400 --> 00:12:04,000
I can do them my own special way.

260
00:12:04,466 --> 00:12:07,733
[narrator] Emily Elephant is Hula-Hooping
with her trunk.

261
00:12:07,800 --> 00:12:09,300
Hooray!

262
00:12:09,366 --> 00:12:12,600
I think that was about 100.

263
00:12:14,666 --> 00:12:17,366
George wants to play leapfrog.

264
00:12:17,433 --> 00:12:19,566
[narrator] George likes playing leapfrog.

265
00:12:20,600 --> 00:12:22,533
Leapfrog, everybody.

266
00:12:24,800 --> 00:12:25,699
One.

267
00:12:25,766 --> 00:12:26,633
Two.

268
00:12:26,699 --> 00:12:27,766
Three.

269
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:28,699
Four.

270
00:12:28,766 --> 00:12:29,633
Five.

271
00:12:29,699 --> 00:12:31,000
Six.

272
00:12:31,066 --> 00:12:32,233
Seven.

273
00:12:32,300 --> 00:12:33,333
Eight.

274
00:12:33,400 --> 00:12:34,400
Nine.

275
00:12:34,466 --> 00:12:35,333
Ten.

276
00:12:35,566 --> 00:12:37,433
[oinks then laughs]

277
00:12:38,433 --> 00:12:39,666
[narrator] Playtime is over.

278
00:12:39,733 --> 00:12:41,233
[all laughing]

279
00:12:43,300 --> 00:12:47,266
Madame Gazelle,
we can all count to ten now.

280
00:12:47,333 --> 00:12:48,500
Very good.

281
00:12:48,566 --> 00:12:51,433
But we need to be playing to do it.

282
00:12:51,500 --> 00:12:52,633
Of course.

283
00:12:53,066 --> 00:12:57,533
Richard, Edmond,
bring the extra-long skipping rope.

284
00:12:58,699 --> 00:12:59,599
Hello.

285
00:12:59,666 --> 00:13:02,400
I've come to collect Peppa and George.

286
00:13:02,466 --> 00:13:05,333
-Daddy, you're too early.
-Oh.

287
00:13:05,400 --> 00:13:07,733
Not to worry, you can join in our game.

288
00:13:08,366 --> 00:13:09,633
Oh, okay.

289
00:13:09,699 --> 00:13:12,133
-Is everybody ready?
-Ready.

290
00:13:13,099 --> 00:13:14,566
Counting to ten.

291
00:13:16,366 --> 00:13:17,233
One.

292
00:13:17,433 --> 00:13:18,433
Two.

293
00:13:18,500 --> 00:13:19,466
Three.

294
00:13:19,533 --> 00:13:20,466
Four.

295
00:13:20,533 --> 00:13:21,433
Five.

296
00:13:21,500 --> 00:13:22,500
Six.

297
00:13:22,566 --> 00:13:23,433
Seven.

298
00:13:23,500 --> 00:13:24,533
Eight.

299
00:13:24,599 --> 00:13:25,566
Nine.

300
00:13:25,633 --> 00:13:26,566
Ten!

301
00:13:27,166 --> 00:13:29,033
[panting]

302
00:13:29,333 --> 00:13:31,500
Oh, you look tired, Daddy Pig.

303
00:13:31,566 --> 00:13:32,733
[chuckles]

304
00:13:32,800 --> 00:13:34,366
I'm fine.

305
00:13:34,633 --> 00:13:36,566
I could skip to 100.

306
00:13:36,633 --> 00:13:38,199
Good idea, Daddy Pig.

307
00:13:38,433 --> 00:13:40,166
To 100.

308
00:13:40,233 --> 00:13:42,533
Uh... Maybe to 20.

309
00:13:42,599 --> 00:13:45,066
Okay. To 20.

310
00:13:45,733 --> 00:13:47,766
Eleven, twelve...

311
00:13:49,400 --> 00:13:52,199
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

312
00:13:52,266 --> 00:13:54,333
[narrator] It is a lovely sunny day.

313
00:13:54,666 --> 00:13:58,066
Peppa and her family are driving
to the playground.

314
00:13:58,166 --> 00:13:59,800
Is everybody ready?

315
00:14:00,033 --> 00:14:01,366
Yes, Daddy Pig.

316
00:14:01,433 --> 00:14:03,400
Then let's go.

317
00:14:05,233 --> 00:14:07,300
We're going to the playground

318
00:14:07,766 --> 00:14:09,699
We're going to the playground

319
00:14:09,766 --> 00:14:12,000
-Ha-ha-ha.
-Vroom, vroom.

320
00:14:12,066 --> 00:14:14,699
[narrator] Peppa and George
love going to the playground.

321
00:14:16,066 --> 00:14:18,599
Oh, why have we stopped?

322
00:14:18,666 --> 00:14:20,300
It's a traffic jam.

323
00:14:20,366 --> 00:14:24,133
But we need to get to the playground.

324
00:14:24,199 --> 00:14:26,000
[crying]

325
00:14:26,066 --> 00:14:30,000
Don't worry, George.
The traffic is moving again.

326
00:14:30,466 --> 00:14:31,366
Stop.

327
00:14:31,433 --> 00:14:33,433
[narrator]
Mr. Bull has stopped the traffic.

328
00:14:33,500 --> 00:14:35,300
What's the problem, Mr. Bull?

329
00:14:35,366 --> 00:14:38,300
Moo! We're digging up the road.

330
00:14:38,766 --> 00:14:42,733
There's water coming out of the ground.

331
00:14:42,800 --> 00:14:46,500
Yes, that's what we're here to fix.

332
00:14:46,566 --> 00:14:48,766
-Ooh.
-Is it going to take long?

333
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:51,699
It will take as long as it takes.

334
00:14:55,800 --> 00:14:57,233
Digger, digger.

335
00:14:57,300 --> 00:14:58,699
[narrator] George likes diggers.

336
00:14:58,766 --> 00:15:01,099
This way, Mr. Rhino.

337
00:15:01,166 --> 00:15:02,500
Okay, boss.

338
00:15:02,566 --> 00:15:04,366
[narrator] Mr. Bull is the boss.

339
00:15:06,633 --> 00:15:09,800
Mr. Bull, where's all that water
coming from?

340
00:15:10,033 --> 00:15:15,233
It's coming from a broken water pipe
underground.

341
00:15:15,300 --> 00:15:19,433
-How are you going to fix it?
-We dig up the road.

342
00:15:22,466 --> 00:15:23,699
Wow!

343
00:15:24,366 --> 00:15:26,366
We turn the water off.

344
00:15:30,633 --> 00:15:33,000
[narrator] George loves cranes.

345
00:15:33,066 --> 00:15:34,666
Crane. Crane.

346
00:15:34,733 --> 00:15:37,266
We take the old pipe out...

347
00:15:37,400 --> 00:15:38,800
[grunting]

348
00:15:40,166 --> 00:15:41,699
and put the new one in.

349
00:15:45,800 --> 00:15:48,133
Thank you for showing us
your work, Mr. Bull.

350
00:15:48,199 --> 00:15:50,500
Moo! No problem.

351
00:15:51,066 --> 00:15:53,466
Bye. See you later.

352
00:15:54,566 --> 00:15:56,033
[crying]

353
00:15:56,099 --> 00:15:59,300
[narrator] Oh, dear.
George doesn't want to leave Mr. Bull.

354
00:15:59,366 --> 00:16:02,400
We're going to the playground, George.

355
00:16:03,699 --> 00:16:06,800
You can play diggers and cranes
in the sandpit.

356
00:16:07,033 --> 00:16:10,666
And we'll see Mr. Bull again
on our way home.

357
00:16:13,500 --> 00:16:16,666
[narrator] Peppa and her family
have arrived at the playground.

358
00:16:18,599 --> 00:16:20,099
Hello, everyone.

359
00:16:20,166 --> 00:16:21,366
Hello, Peppa.

360
00:16:22,433 --> 00:16:26,266
[narrator] Edmond Elephant and
Richard Rabbit are playing in the sandpit.

361
00:16:26,333 --> 00:16:28,199
[all mimicking engine noises]

362
00:16:32,066 --> 00:16:33,633
Let's play in the sandpit.

363
00:16:33,699 --> 00:16:34,666
-Okay.
-Okay.

364
00:16:36,533 --> 00:16:37,400
Stop.

365
00:16:37,666 --> 00:16:39,333
What's the problem?

366
00:16:39,566 --> 00:16:44,099
We're digging up the road,
and I'm the boss.

367
00:16:44,166 --> 00:16:45,199
Oh.

368
00:16:48,099 --> 00:16:50,066
Is it going to take long?

369
00:16:50,533 --> 00:16:53,699
It will take as long as it will take.

370
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:55,766
We have to make a hole.

371
00:16:58,133 --> 00:16:59,433
We fill it in...

372
00:17:02,133 --> 00:17:04,066
and the road is mended.

373
00:17:04,133 --> 00:17:05,533
Hooray!

374
00:17:05,599 --> 00:17:07,399
[all laughing]

375
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:11,033
Peppa, George, it's time to go home.

376
00:17:11,099 --> 00:17:12,399
-Oh.
-Wah!

377
00:17:12,466 --> 00:17:15,500
[narrator] Oh, dear.
George doesn't want to go home yet.

378
00:17:15,566 --> 00:17:20,033
On the way home, George,
we can see Mr. Bull digging up the road.

379
00:17:20,800 --> 00:17:22,166
Bye, everyone.

380
00:17:22,233 --> 00:17:23,399
Bye, Peppa.

381
00:17:26,533 --> 00:17:30,766
[narrator] Peppa and George are looking
forward to seeing Mr. Bull again.

382
00:17:31,399 --> 00:17:32,733
Digger. Crane.

383
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:36,100
Here we are. Oh.

384
00:17:36,333 --> 00:17:38,233
[narrator] Mr. Bull is not here.

385
00:17:38,300 --> 00:17:41,200
Mr. Bull must have finished and gone home.

386
00:17:41,266 --> 00:17:43,066
[crying]

387
00:17:43,133 --> 00:17:44,633
[engines roaring]

388
00:17:47,566 --> 00:17:49,133
Digger. Crane!

389
00:17:50,433 --> 00:17:52,500
Moo! Stop.

390
00:17:53,266 --> 00:17:55,733
Oh, is the water pipe broken again?

391
00:17:55,800 --> 00:18:00,600
No, Peppa.
This time, it's faulty electrical cables.

392
00:18:00,666 --> 00:18:04,100
How to you mend "ecleckity clables"?

393
00:18:04,166 --> 00:18:06,466
We dig up the road!

394
00:18:06,533 --> 00:18:07,566
Hooray!

395
00:18:08,600 --> 00:18:12,133
[narrator] Peppa and George love it
when Mr. Bull digs up the road.

396
00:18:13,033 --> 00:18:16,433
Everyone loves it
when Mr. Bull digs up the road.

397
00:18:16,566 --> 00:18:18,666
[horns honking]

